# The same working directory is sometimes seen AT THE SAME TIME by two systems: Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true) and Linux. So the same file is run by /bin/sh on the host and by Git
# Bash on Windows. Without forcing LF, a checkout on the Windows side would insert CRLF, and
# the host would fail with "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
*.sh                text eol=lf

# The probe is sometimes compared byte for byte against the copy handed out to the machines.
# Differing line endings would turn that into a false alarm on every comparison.
*.py                text eol=lf
